+# FAA correspondence film inventory, inspections and transfer records
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · **B129 / PD01–PD05**. The FAA micrographics order and the 2002 federal microform provisions identify records that could locate a retained correspondence copy after a paper file was filmed. The important distinction is between an equipment inventory, a film-series inventory, a transfer to storage and a transfer of legal custody. The 1985 FAA correspondence manual, the case’s film or electronic control entry, and the signed 2006 response remain unacquired. [Earlier correspondence and delivery review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/7dcb6c28f8c4496148f11406570140b3c18e9eda/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-correspondence-predecessor-and-mail-controls-2026-11-08/README.md) · [Source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Records that would identify a copy or its custodian
+
+| Source and locator | Record to seek and what it would establish |
+| --- | --- |
+| **FAA 1350.20B**, PDF pp. 2–3, §§10–11 | The order specifies inventories of equipment and optical disk systems and names **FAA Form 1350-5** for a system proposal. It calls for approval of proposed systems involving disposal after conversion. Seek the proposal, approval, inventory and office assignment for the specific correspondence system. An equipment inventory leaves the contents of particular rolls or disks open. [FAA order, p. 3](https://www.faa.gov/documentLibrary/media/Order/ND/1350.20B.pdf#page=3) |
+| **36 CFR §1230.22(c), (e)**, May 14 PDF p. 5 lines 54–78 | The film inventory includes series, production date, producer, processor, format and prior inspection results. The inspection report calls for batches by year and roll or fiche identifiers, with separate detailed logs. Seek the series-level entries covering the relevant dates and the actual inspection and corrective-action records. These fields could connect a control entry to a particular unit of film. [May 14 republication, p. 5](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2002-05-14/pdf/R2-10588.pdf#page=5) |
+| **§1230.28(c)**, May 14 PDF pp. 5–6, lines 120–130 and 3–5 | The storage transmittal, **SF 135** for a NARA records center, or its attachment carries office, title, medium, film-unit ID, date coverage, and finding aids and inspection documentation. Seek the transmittal and actual receipt. This is the storage stage. [Transmittal fields](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2002-05-14/pdf/R2-10588.pdf#page=5) |
+| **§1230.30**, May 14 PDF p. 6 lines 12–27 | The legal custody procedure separately names **SF 258** unless NARA instructs otherwise, with film copies and current inspection. Seek the actual signed transfer agreement and accession inventory, or the successor record if another process applied. An approved procedure leaves execution and item-level coverage open. [Legal custody fields](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2002-05-14/pdf/R2-10588.pdf#page=6) |
+
+The earlier FAA correspondence study records **AOA-3** and the 2000 description of permanent correspondence film. Use the target answer or report date, addressee, subject and control number to identify an indexed series before seeking the exact roll, frame or later migrated object. A surviving copy would still require a separate match to its approved version and delivery evidence. The FAA’s **1350.23** microform catalog has public metadata and the page says its body is unavailable. Its coverage of the 1985 manual and the target correspondence remains unverified. [Correspondence-control crosswalk](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2b030c70ecb95e0929661ba04df3e039b4db6942/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-aoa3-correspondence-control-2026-11-06/README.md) · [FAA microform catalog record](https://www.faa.gov/regulations_policies/orders_notices/index.cfm/go/document.information/documentID/6840)
+
+## Wording and edition differences retained
+
+- The May 9 and May 14 Federal Register bodies have separate print dates, pagination and hashes. Both give **June 10, 2002** as the effective date. The May 14 editor’s note describes a republication in a different format and says the format changes do not affect legal status. The July 1, 2002 CFR extract is a third representation. Preserve each as acquired. [May 9 original issue, p. 1](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2002-05-09/pdf/02-10588.pdf#page=1) · [May 14 republication, p. 1](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2002-05-14/pdf/R2-10588.pdf#page=1) · [2002 CFR extract](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CFR-2002-title36-vol3/pdf/CFR-2002-title36-vol3-part1230.pdf)
+- The May 14 preamble says **“produced during or after 1990”**. The regulatory text on p. 5 says **“produced after 1990”**. The same distinction appears in the May 9 body, and the CFR extract preserves the latter wording. This review leaves the 1990 boundary and any applicable correction open. [Preamble](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2002-05-14/pdf/R2-10588.pdf#page=1) · [Inspection rule](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2002-05-14/pdf/R2-10588.pdf#page=5)
+- The three publications’ storage-transmittal clause points to **§1230.22(a) (5) and (6)** for inspection forms and reports. The inspected text of **§1230.22(a)** lists items **(1)–(4)** in all three. The separately printed **§1230.22(e)** describes an inspection report and log. The printed cross-reference and paragraph labels are preserved without substituting a target. [May 9 p. 6](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2002-05-09/pdf/02-10588.pdf#page=6) · [May 14 p. 6](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2002-05-14/pdf/R2-10588.pdf#page=6) · [CFR p. 9](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CFR-2002-title36-vol3/pdf/CFR-2002-title36-vol3-part1230.pdf#page=9)
+- FAA 1350.20B’s cancellation paragraph describes predecessor **1350.20A** as dated **December 12, 1981**. The FAA catalog labels that predecessor’s issue date **1981-12-01**. The 1987 order also cites **1350.21A**. The FAA catalog separately gives that standards order a **1989-09-01** cancellation and points to **1350.21B**. The bodies and applicable changes to the predecessor and standards remain separate retrieval targets. [FAA order p. 1](https://www.faa.gov/documentLibrary/media/Order/ND/1350.20B.pdf#page=1) · [Predecessor catalog](https://www.faa.gov/regulations_policies/orders_notices/index.cfm/go/document.information/documentID/6835) · [Standards catalog](https://www.faa.gov/regulations_policies/orders_notices/index.cfm/go/document.information/documentID/6837)
+
+**Next test.** Join the actual AOA-3 control number to the film-series inventory or electronic migration mapping, then to the transfer and exact image or file. Determine which authority, edition and schedule applied to that series and whether the transfer was executed. The corrected answer and recipient acknowledgment, signed action or no-action decision, and each recommendation’s disposition remain outstanding. [2006 OIG report, pp. 12–13](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=12)
+
+Verification covered four acquired PDF bodies, **34 physical pages**, **32** exact text locators and three numbered-row checks. Selected cross-references, wording and the FAA form label were checked on source images. No actual correspondence film, dispatch, administrative decision or case-level retention event was verified. [Verification scope](SOURCE-PINS.json)
